syntax:
declaration:
    decl-specifier-seq declarator-listopt init-declarator-listopt ;

Implementation notes: The decl-specifier-seq includes elements like storage-class-specifier (e.g., 'static'), type-specifier (e.g., 'int', 'class Foo'), and function-specifier (e.g., 'inline'). The compiler first parses this sequence to deduce the type, then applies it to the declarator (e.g., 'x' in 'int x;'). For example, in 'const int x;', the compiler flags 'const' as a cv-qualifier in the seq, affecting memory access (read-only in some contexts) and potentially generating assembly with load instructions that respect volatility or constancy.
